messages.reasoning:
Now I see the full hermes.upshalter.com config. The server block on line 1 handles hermes.upshalter.com on port 443 (SSL). It has:

- location = / → root /var/www/hermes-dashboard
- location /main, /upshalternal, /agent1, /agent2, /agent3 → proxy to respective ports
- location /workstation → alias /root/workstation
- location /workspace/ → proxy to 3000 (line 90)
- No location /hermes/ for static files
- No location /kanban/ for proxy to 3001
- No location /api/ for proxy to 8000
- No location /ws for WebSocket

The user's memory says the base path is /hermes/ with sub-paths: /hermes/ (static HTML at /var/www/workstation/hermes/), /hermes/workspace/ (proxy 3000), /hermes/kanban/ (proxy 3001), /hermes/api/* (proxy 8000 + API key), /hermes/ws (WebSocket).

So we need to add these location blocks to the server block (lines 1-104) in hermes.upshalter.com config:

1. location /hermes/ → serve static files from /var/www/workstation/hermes/ (since the root for /hermes/ is /var/www/workstation/hermes/, so the location /hermes/ would map to that root, with try_files $uri $uri/ =404;)

Wait, the root for the server is not set, but the location = / uses root /var/www/hermes-dashboard. To serve /hermes/ static files from /var/www/workstation/hermes/, we can add:

location /hermes/ {
    alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/;
    try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
}

Because using alias instead of root, since the location is /hermes/ and the files are in /var/www/workstation/hermes/ (so /hermes/lobby/index.html maps to /var/www/workstation/hermes/lobby/index.html).

Then add location /hermes/kanban/ to proxy to 3001:

location /hermes/kanban/ {
    rewrite ^/hermes/kanban(/.*)$ $1 break;
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3001;
    # same proxy settings as /workspace/
}

Then location /hermes/api/ to proxy to 8000 with API key:

location /hermes/api/ {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
    proxy_set_header X-API-Key "your-api-key-here"; # need to get the actual API key from user's config
    # proxy settings
}

And location /hermes/ws for WebSocket:

location /hermes/ws {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
    # other headers
